  The engine ships as a single-page HTML file upstream; here its rules, scoring,
  rendering and animation logic were re-expressed as an ES module and its
  stylesheet was scoped to the OS window. Every adaptation and every improvement
  over upstream is listed in solitaire-aashish/README.md.

  No card artwork is bundled: the deck is drawn with CSS and Unicode suit
  glyphs, so there is no third-party card library in the package.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Keyboard easter eggs (public/react-pwa.js)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The "type pikachu / mario / ohhh" amusements are adapted from the
  easter-egg-collection by Wei-Chia Chang (MIT):
  https://github.com/WeiChiaChang/easter-egg-collection

  They are loaded lazily, after the desktop is on screen, so they never sit on
  the boot path.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Previously used components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

An earlier build of this project shipped a hand-written Klondike engine, then a
port of cango91/solitaire. Neither is registered as the active Solitaire engine in v1.02. Some legacy source/assets remain in the repository for reference and attribution; the current engine (above) is the active replacement.

